(RUNBOOK - running and rescuing the Purchasing system) Tj T*
(Audience: whoever ends up responsible for this app after the person who built it stops touching it.) Tj T*
(You do not need to understand Laravel. You need to follow the checklists and respect one rule: never change the server before making a fresh back-up.) Tj T*
(Everything else is details, and the details are all here.) Tj T*
(Works with: `README.md` \(install & architecture\), `docs/Teaching-Guide-Purchasing-System.md` \(staff training\).) Tj T*
(---) Tj T*
(0. The five things to know up front) Tj T*
(1. This app runs entirely on one machine on the office LAN. There is no cloud component. If that machine dies, the app is down until it is restored - this is acceptable by design, provided you keep back-ups \(see §2\).) Tj T*
(2. Nothing in the app requires the internet \(as of 2026-11 the Tailwind CDN was removed; see §7\). You can unplug the network cable from the server and the app still works.) Tj T*
(3. Upgrades are optional, not routine. Do not update PHP, MySQL/MariaDB, XAMPP, or `composer` packages "to stay current" - an unmanaged box is safer frozen. Upgrade only when the hardware itself is replaced \(see §4\).) Tj T*
(4. Every incident follows one shape: restore from back-up, then verify, then fix. Never improvise on the only copy of the data.) Tj T*
(5. The database back-up contains only the database. The uploaded supplier quotation files live in a separate folder and must be backed up separately \(see §2\).) Tj T*
(---) Tj T*
(1. Where everything lives) Tj T*
(| Thing | Path \(default layout\) |) Tj T*
(|---|---|) Tj T*
(| Application code | `C:\\...\\purchasing\\` \(the repo\) |) Tj T*
(| Environment \(DB password, APP_KEY\) | `purchasing\\.env` - not in git; keep a sealed copy with the back-ups |) Tj T*
(| Database | MySQL/MariaDB, database `purchasing_db`, user `root` \(localhost-only\) |) Tj T*
(| DB back-ups \(in-app\) | `purchasing\\storage\\app\\private\\backups\\*.sql` \(keeps the 15 newest\) |) Tj T*
(| Uploaded quotation files | `purchasing\\storage\\app\\private\\quotations\\` |) Tj T*
(| Logs | `purchasing\\storage\\logs\\laravel.log` |) Tj T*
(| Schedule runner | Windows Task Scheduler or cron: `php artisan schedule:run` every minute \(runs `activity:prune` weekly\) |) Tj T*
(If your layout differs, adjust the paths - but keep the discipline: code, env, DB, uploads, logs.) Tj T*
(---) Tj T*
(2. The weekly 10-minute back-up \(all of it, every time\)) Tj T*
(Do this every week, on the same day:) Tj T*
(1. Sign in to the app as an Administrator -> Settings -> Backup -> Create backup.) Tj T*
(2. Wait for the new row in the back-up list. Note the filename.) Tj T*
(3. Copy to a USB stick / second PC / network share:) Tj T*
(o the newest `.sql` from `storage\\app\\private\\backups\\` and) Tj T*
(o the whole folder `storage\\app\\private\\quotations\\` and) Tj T*
(o `purchasing\\.env` \(fresh copy - the APP_KEY never changes, but keep it current\)) Tj T*
(4. Put the USB in a known drawer. Label it with the date.) Tj T*
(> The in-app back-up alone can resurrect the database but not the supplier files the procurement cycle ran on. USB with only the database = half a restore.) Tj T*
(The in-app list keeps the 15 newest back-ups; the USB keeps everything.) Tj T*
(---) Tj T*
(3. Monthly 2-minute health check) Tj T*
(1. Can you open `http://<server-ip>/login` from a different PC? \(Checks Apache/MySQL are alive.\)) Tj T*
(2. On the server: is there at least 10% free disk space? \(`C:\\` drive -> Properties.\)) Tj T*
(3. Settings -> Logs - does the newest entry look recent? \(Confirms the app is running and the schedule is alive.\)) Tj T*
(4. Is the newest USB back-up younger than 14 days? If not, make one now.) Tj T*
(If any of these fails, see §5.) Tj T*
(---) Tj T*
(4. Replacing the server \(the 3-5 year reality\)) Tj T*
(The one failure you cannot script around is the PC itself dying. When that happens, or when you replace it:) Tj T*
(1. Get a replacement machine \(any modern Windows PC is fine\).) Tj T*
(2. Install the same or newer XAMPP \(PHP >= 8.2, MySQL/MariaDB, Apache\). Do not chase exact versions.) Tj T*
ET
endstream
